{"uid":"modules/obs_parser.py","name":"obs_parser.py","qualname":"modules/obs_parser.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/obs_parser.py","line":1,"end_line":570,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"modules/obs_parser.py ====================== Observation parser: extracts structured findings from raw tool output.","description":"Converts unstructured text (nmap, gobuster, crackmapexec, enum4linux, etc.)\ninto typed Finding objects that the WorldModel can ingest directly.\n\nExtractors are independent, additive, and follow Open/Closed:\n  - Add a new extractor by subclassing Extractor and registering it.\n  - Existing extractors are never modified to support new patterns.\n\nDesign\n------\n- Single Responsibility : each Extractor owns one finding type\n- Open/Closed           : new types via new Extractor subclass\n- Liskov                : all Extractor subclasses honour the same contract\n- Interface Segregation : consumers only see FindingType, Finding, Observation\n- Dependency Inversion  : ObsParser depends on Extractor abstraction\n\nUsage\n-----\n    from modules.obs_parser import ObsParser\n\n    parser = ObsParser()\n    obs    = parser.parse(nmap_output, host=\"10.10.11.78\", tool=\"nmap\")\n\n    for finding in obs.findings:\n        print(finding.type, finding.value, finding.confidence)","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/obs_parser.py::FindingType","modules/obs_parser.py::Finding","modules/obs_parser.py::Observation","modules/obs_parser.py::Extractor","modules/obs_parser.py::ObsParser","modules/obs_parser.py::get_parser","modules/obs_parser.py::parse"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
